lok: a part not shown paints aside, the shown slide untouched

doc_paintPartTile paints a part other than the shown one by switching
the only view to it and back (doc_setPartImpl with bAllowChangeFocus
false, which only this path uses). In Impress that is a full
DrawViewShell::SwitchPage both ways: SdrMarkView::HideSdrPage drops
every mark of the shown slide, the frame view's selected page and the
page selection flags change, in-place objects are disconnected, the
visible area is reset, the form shell is closed and FireSwitchCurrentPage
tells every listener. The user's selection was gone after any thumbnail
of another slide (Ely R19.5: ElyShow paints a slide's thumbnail when an
edit lands on it; play_time::back_shows_a_slide_fully_built_even_
without_clicks failed every time).

ITiledRenderable::setPaintPart(nPart, nMode) asks the document to
paint that part instead of the shown one; -1 ends it. Impress paints
it on a DrawView of its own, as the slide sorter's PreviewRenderer
does, with the shown view's page, border, grid, layer and help line
settings and its document color, so the picture matches the slide
painted while shown. Nothing of the shown view changes. Slides,
masters and notes pages are painted this way; a document that
declines (Calc) is switched as before. Form controls are drawn
through controls made for the shown view's window, so a slide not
shown paints them as the slide sorter does.

